# The Python tools in the gcc-arm-11.3 image: the versions firmware projects
# used on Ubuntu 18.04 (Python 3.6), kept wherever they work on Ubuntu 22.04's
# Python 3.10. requirements.txt is compiled from this file and pins every
# package, dependencies too, with its SHA-256; recompile it after a change:
#
#   cd images/gcc-arm-11.3
#   uv pip compile --python-version 3.10 --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu \
#     --generate-hashes --no-header --emit-index-url \
#     --build-constraint build-constraints.txt -o requirements.txt requirements.in
#
# Moved up from the 18.04 versions, each to the oldest release that works on 3.10:
#   heatshrink2  0.9.0 → 0.11.0  0.9.0's generated C doesn't build on 3.10;
#                                0.11.0 is the same source, regenerated
#   intelHex     2.2.1 → 2.3.0   2.2.1 calls array.tostring, gone in 3.9
#   mypy         0.782 → 0.910   0.782 needs typed-ast < 1.5, which doesn't
#                                load on 3.10 and breaks black
#   pytest       5.4.2 → 6.2.5   older releases fail on 3.10 ("required field
#                                lineno missing from alias")

